{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the king said, etc.</b> Even though the entire matter recounted in the subject uses plural language — as it is written ״וַיָּשִׂימוּ״ (they set), ״וְכַאֲשֶׁר יְעַנּוּ״ (so they afflicted), etc., ״וַיַּעֲבִידוּ״ (they made serve), ״וַיְמָרְרוּ״ (they embittered) — for it was not the king alone who acted but he and his people, this particular deed the king did alone, so that the matter would remain secret — so that the Hebrew women would not take notice to hide their pregnancies, and so that they would not keep the midwives away from delivering them, as I shall explain below." "<b>To the midwives of the Hebrews, etc.</b> One must examine what he said to them with this statement. And perhaps the statement is that he called and said <b>the Hebrew women, of whom the name of the one</b>, etc. — for since many came before him and he did not know which were the midwives, therefore he called them by name to direct his speech specifically to them, inasmuch as they were the superiors over all the midwives, and he wished to lay the matter upon them, for so is the way of authority. It further intends that he made them superiors and officers over all the midwives through this calling, and that is why he specified their names, and therefore he went back to say a second time <b>and he said, When you deliver</b>, etc. — meaning that the command was not to those two alone but to all the midwives, except that these two would be officers over them." "It further alludes to a language of greatness and exaltation, after the manner of (Deuteronomy 26:17–18): ״אֶת ה׳ הֶאֱמַרְתָּ וַה׳ הֶאֱמִירְךָ״ (you have declared HaShem … and HaShem has declared you), and the intention in this is to tell that through the intermediacy of this matter Pharaoh brought about elevation and exaltation for the two midwives, and they rose in rank as stated nearby (Exodus 1:20): ״וַיֵּיטֶב אֱלֹהִים וְגוֹ׳ וַיַּעַשׂ לָהֶם בָּתִּים״ — houses of priesthood, houses of levitical service, houses of royalty, houses of prophecy (Sotah 11a)."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:08.798115535Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}